# Shared TypeScript Configuration Package

This package provides shared TypeScript configurations (tsconfig.json) for different parts of the monorepo, ensuring consistent type checking and compilation settings.

## Purpose

Centralize TypeScript compiler options to maintain type safety and consistency across:
- Next.js apps (web, desktop, docs)
- Electron main process
- React Native/Expo apps
- Node.js packages
- React libraries

## Structure

```
packages/typescript-config/
├── base.json               # Base TypeScript configuration
├── nextjs.json             # Next.js-specific config
├── node.json               # Node.js-specific config
├── electron.json           # Electron-specific config
├── expo.json               # Expo/React Native config
├── react-library.json      # React library config
├── backend.json            # Backend/server config
├── package.json
└── README.md
```

## Configuration Files

### Base Configuration (`base.json`)
- Shared compiler options
- Common type checking rules
- Base paths and references
- Target and module settings

### Next.js Configuration (`nextjs.json`)
- Extends base config
- Next.js-specific settings
- App Router support
- React Server Components types

### Electron Configuration (`electron.json`)
- Electron main process settings
- Node.js types
- Electron-specific types

### Expo Configuration (`expo.json`)
- React Native types
- Expo SDK types
- Mobile platform types

### Node.js Configuration (`node.json`)
- Node.js backend settings
- CommonJS/ESM support
- Server-side types

### React Library Configuration (`react-library.json`)
- React component library settings
- JSX support
- Library distribution types

## Usage

### In tsconfig.json
```json
{
  "extends": "@repo/typescript-config/nextjs",
  "compilerOptions": {
    // Override specific options if needed
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules"]
}
```

## TypeScript Best Practices

### Configuration
- Always extend base config
- Override only when necessary
- Use strict mode
- Enable all useful checks

### Type Safety
- Use strict TypeScript settings
- Enable no implicit any
- Use proper type imports
- Leverage type inference

### Paths and References
- Use path aliases consistently
- Set up project references for monorepo
- Configure module resolution correctly

## Integration

### Consuming Packages
- Apps extend appropriate config
- Packages use base or specific config
- Override locally if needed
- Keep consistent across monorepo

### Maintenance
- Update TypeScript regularly
- Review compiler options
- Test in all consuming apps
- Maintain compatibility

## Important Notes

- Changes affect all consuming apps
- Test compiler option changes
- Maintain backward compatibility
- Document configuration options
- Keep configs focused and consistent

### Common Patterns
- Strict mode enabled
- Modern target (ESNext)
- Module resolution: Bundler
- Type checking enabled
- Path aliases for monorepo
